@title Dispatch queue backed up
@subtitle On-call runbook for the dispatch-jobs queue, Quickpost Couriers
@author Dispatch Engineering

kpi Alert threshold | 5,000 | for 10 minutes | bad
kpi Normal depth | under 400 | good
kpi DB pool cap | 200 connections
kpi Max consumers | 40

## Symptoms

- The `QUEUE_DEPTH_HIGH` alert fires when depth stays above 5000 for 10 minutes. Normal is under 400.
- Drivers see new jobs arrive late in the app.

## Diagnose

- Check queue depth and consumer count with `kubectl -n dispatch get hpa dispatch-consumer`.
- Look at the oldest message age on the queue dashboard.
- Check the database connection pool, which is capped at 200 connections.

## Fix steps

!!! Never purge dispatch-jobs. Every message is a real customer delivery.

1. Scale the consumers.
-- 1. Run `kubectl -n dispatch scale deploy dispatch-consumer --replicas=24`.
-- 2. Wait 5 minutes and re-check.
-- 3. If depth is still rising, scale to 40, the maximum the database pool supports.
2. Check for poison messages.
-- 1. Look for any message retried more than 10 times.
-- 2. Move it to `dispatch-dlq` with the `dlq-move` tool.
3. Pause the bulk import scheduler in the admin console. Bulk imports add up to 3000 jobs at a time.
4. When depth drops under 400, re-enable the scheduler gradually.

## Escalation

If depth is still above 5000 after 20 minutes, page the Dispatch Engineering lead and open an incident in #incidents.
